    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` to the v2 paginated API.\n\n**Changes**\n- Uses `POST /v2/graphql` with `settlements(first, after)`.\n- Follows `pageInfo.hasNextPage` until exhausted, tolerating short and empty pages.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last delivered version while preserving first-delivery order.\n- Retries `429` with `Retry-After`, resending the identical request.\n- Restarts from the beginning on an invalid/expired cursor, whether reported as a GraphQL error or an HTTP error body.\n- Guards against a cursor that does not advance.\n\n**Verified against `http://the VM's public address:18081`**\n- Reconciled **1,873 settlements**, all with unique IDs.\n- Independent v2 traversal with a different page size produced the same IDs, objects, and ordering.\n- Output matched the still-live v1 ledger exactly, including the 19 amended settlements.\n- Local edge-case tests passed for `429`, empty/short pages, amending duplicates, and cursor restart on both `200` and `400` responses.",
